<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh tea prices rise at first sale of season.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh tea prices rise at first sale of season.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladeshi teas fetched higher prices on overseas and local demand at the first auction of the season, brokers said.</p>
<p>Brokers said the prices advanced sharply immediately after the opening of the auction on Tuesday as buyers for Pakistan, Poland and Afghanistan operated strongly.</p>
<p>The average price was 63.63 taka per kilo compared with 46.64 taka in the last auction held on March 18.</p>
<p>Some 1.2 million kg of teas were sold in the auction. The next sale will be on May 20 when 925,000 kg of teas will be on offer. ($1 = 43.65 taka)</p>
</text>
